  "tier": "well-attested",
  "plain": "In 2023 a whistleblower named David Grusch testified before the US Congress about UFOs, and part of what he knew could only be shared in secret. That kind of briefing has to happen in a SCIF, a specially secured room for handling classified information. Grusch says the members of Congress were furious because, as he understood it, they couldn't reserve one for his classified briefing in Washington. A second account comes from an unnamed speaker who seems to be one of those members. This person tells it first-hand and goes further, saying flatly that \"we were denied access\" to the room. If true, it would suggest that someone inside the system was trying to keep lawmakers from hearing what Grusch had to say."
}
